From b904e32e28649ee19e580b5b008c69e4454cf4b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Zegalia <ryanzegalia@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:38:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add a switch-pro target: wired Nintendo Switch Pro
 Controller over uhid

Presents the composite device to Steam and games as a Pro Controller
(057e:2009, USB), so Steam and controller-type-aware games draw Nintendo
glyphs. Answers the host protocol Steam (SDL_hidapi_switch.c) and the
kernel's hid-nintendo run before a Pro Controller streams input: USB 0x80
status/handshake/baudrate/no-timeout, subcommands device info, input mode,
SPI flash reads (factory stick + IMU calibration, colours, stick params;
user calibration reads as erased), SPI writes kept in memory, IMU,
vibration, player/home lights, regulated voltage; every other subcommand
is ACKed so no host stalls. Streams the 0x30 full report every 4 ms with
12-bit sticks and three IMU samples. Rumble (0x01/0x10 bytes 2-9) decodes
to a GenericRumble event. Face buttons map by label (South=A, East=B,
West=X, North=Y); QuickAccess = Steam's Guide+A chord; analog triggers
become digital ZL/ZR with hysteresis.
